:PATH
Section 1 General Provisions
|

:INFO
Art. 18 Definitions
1 An initial survey is the production of the components of official cadastral surveying in areas that have not been previously subject to a fully approved cadastral survey and in areas defined in Article 51 paragraphs 3 and 4.
2 Finalisation is defined as the revision or expansion of a fully recognised official cadastral survey in order to adapt it to current regulations.
3 Updating is the modification of the components of official cadastral surveying to reflect changes in the legal or factual circumstances.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529).
|

:INFO
Art. 19 Procedures
The Federal Directorate of Cadastral Surveying may issue directives concerning methods for initial survey, finalisation and updating.
|

:NOTE
Name in accordance with No I of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529). This amendment has been made throughout the document.
|

:INFO
Art. 20 Geodetic reference system
The position and height references for official cadastral surveying are governed by Articles 4 and 5 GeoIO.
|

:NOTE
Art. 20 — Amended by No I of the O of 21 May 2008, in force since 1 July 2008 (AS 2008 2745).
SR 510.620
|

:INFO
Art. 21 Schedule for surveying
1 The Federal Directorate of Cadastral Surveying and the competent cantonal authority shall plan official cadastral surveying on the basis of a programme agreement.
2 The canton shall determine when individual surveys are to be carried out. It shall regulate the consultation procedure.
3 …
